---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StepsStrip from '../components/StepsStrip.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'What does flattening do?',
    a: 'A filled form keeps its answers in editable fields, which some printers, portals and older readers display wrongly or not at all. Flattening bakes the answers into the pages themselves, so the file shows the same thing everywhere and the answers can no longer be edited by accident.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What about highlights and sticky notes?',
    a: 'They are annotations, not form fields, and this engine cannot bake them into the page. The page counts them and the result line reports them, in the open, rather than dropping them silently. They remain annotations in the finished file.',
  },
  {
    q: 'My PDF has no form fields. What happens?',
    a: 'The page finds none, says so before you run, and if you run it anyway your file comes back re-saved with the result line stating that nothing was flattened. Nothing is dressed up.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my document go?',
    a: 'Nowhere. It is read into this page and flattened in your browser. Watch the network panel while it works if you want to check.',
  },
];
const faqJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
});
const howToJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: "How to flatten a PDF form",
  step: [
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 1, name: "Pick the filled form", text: "Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one. It stays on this device. The page counts its form fields and other annotations before anything runs." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 2, name: "Flatten the PDF", text: "Press 'Flatten the PDF'. Each field's value is drawn into its page as ordinary content, and the field itself is removed." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 3, name: "Check the result line", text: "The result reports the finished file's own numbers: fields flattened, fields left (zero), and any non-field annotations counted and named as not baked in." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 4, name: "Download the flattened PDF", text: "Take the finished file away. Keep your editable original if you may need to change the answers later." },
  ],
});
---

<Base title="Flatten PDF: bake form answers into the pages, free · Benchzy" description="Flatten a filled PDF form so its answers become part of the pages, inside your browser. Non-field annotations are counted and reported, never silently dropped.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">PDF tools · forms</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">Flatten PDF</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        The finishing step for a filled form: bake the answers into the pages, so the file
        prints and displays the same everywhere and nobody can change a field by accident.
        Everything runs in your browser; the document is never uploaded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-6 p-5 sm:p-7" id="fl-tool">
      <div id="fl-tray" class="tray p-6 text-center cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Pick a PDF">
        <p class="font-display text-xl font-bold">Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one</p>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft mt-2">PDF · it stays on this device</p>
        <input id="fl-file" type="file" accept="application/pdf,.pdf" class="hidden" />
      </div>
      <p class="file-loaded hidden" data-loaded-for="fl-file" role="status"></p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 mt-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_320px]">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">What gets flattened</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft text-sm leading-relaxed mt-3 max-w-md">
            Form fields (text boxes, checkboxes, dropdowns, radio buttons) are baked into the
            pages. Other annotations are counted on the spec and reported on the result line;
            this page does not hide them and does not remove them. Keep your editable
            original: flattening is a one-way door for the fields.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">File spec</h2>
          <dl id="fl-spec" class="mt-2">
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>file</dt><dd>none picked yet</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="action-note">
            One warning before you run it: flattening is a one-way door for the fields. Once it
            runs, the answers are part of the page and cannot be edited as fields again, so keep
            your editable original. And if the form has a signature field, flattening bakes
            in whatever that field shows right now. If it is empty or wrong, fix the form first,
            then flatten. Afterwards, open the finished file and check it before you file it.
          </p>
          <button id="fl-run" class="btn-primary w-full mt-5" type="button" disabled>Flatten the PDF</button>
          <p id="fl-status" class="font-mono text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite">Pick a PDF to begin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="fl-result" class="receipt hidden mt-8">
        <div class="tear pt-5 flex items-center gap-4 flex-wrap">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Result</h2>
          <span class="stamp" id="fl-stamp">Done on your device</span>
        </div>
        <p id="fl-achieved" class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl"></p>
        <a id="fl-download" class="btn-primary inline-block no-underline mt-3" href="#" download>Download the flattened PDF</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <StepsStrip who="For a filled form whose answers must stay put when the file is printed, emailed, or opened somewhere else." steps={[{ n: '01', t: 'Pick the filled form' }, { n: '02', t: 'Flatten the PDF' }, { n: '03', t: 'Check and download' }]} />

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">How it works</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The page opens the form, refreshes each field's appearance from its value, and then
          merges the fields into the page content with the PDF engine's own form tools. The
          output is opened again and counted, so the result line reports the finished file's
          numbers (fields left: zero), not the plan.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Honest limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Flattening is final for the fields: the answers become ink, not data, so a flattened
          form cannot be re-filled or machine-read as a form afterwards. Annotations that are
          not form fields are reported, not flattened, per the note on the ticket. A signature
          field flattens to whatever its appearance shows; check the finished file before you
          file it.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A password-protected PDF cannot be opened by this tool. Take its password off first with the <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/unlock-pdf/">unlock tool</a>, then bring the file back.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold">{f.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{f.a}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqJson}></script>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={howToJson}></script>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/flatten-pdf.js';
  </script>
</Base>
